  "goodToKnow": "Schaufeln means to shovel or dig: Schnee schaufeln, Sand schaufeln, ein Loch schaufeln. In many German towns, residents must clear snow from the pavement in front of their house (Räum- und Streupflicht). Sich sein eigenes Grab schaufeln means to dig one's own grave. Die Schaufel is a shovel, and die Schaufelradbagger are the giant excavators of lignite mines. Regular: schaufelte, geschaufelt."
